{"abstract":[{"text":"Send records to PostHog Cloud or a self-hosted PostHog through its batch capture API.","type":"text"}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Sending to PostHog","anchor":"Sending-to-PostHog","identifiers":["doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/postHog(projectToken:host:plan:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/postHog(projectToken:host:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogSetupError"]},{"title":"Encoding batches","anchor":"Encoding-batches","identifiers":["doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogBatchEncoder"]},{"title":"Records left out","anchor":"Records-left-out","identifiers":["doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogEncodingError"]}],"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/postHog(projectToken:host:plan:backoff:clock:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" makes an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":") for your PostHog project in one call. It checks"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the project token and the host, posts to the host’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\/batch\/"},{"type":"text","text":" with a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogBatchEncoder","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"splits each batch to PostHog’s limits ("},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogBatchEncoder\/batchLimit","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"). A batch with no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"record the encoder can write, an empty one included, makes no request. It retries no response, a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"5xx, 408 and 429, and drops and reports any other status. The project token goes in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the body, so no header field is needed, and no trace context is sent. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import Traffluent"},{"type":"text","text":" leaves"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"this module out; import it on its own."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each record becomes an anonymous event. Its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"distinct_id"},{"type":"text","text":" is the record’s session, from the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sessions enricher, also sent as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$session_id"},{"type":"text","text":"; a record with no session is sent under its own"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"record identifier. Its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"uuid"},{"type":"text","text":" is the record’s identifier, which a redelivered record keeps. Every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"event carries "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$process_person_profile: false"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$geoip_disable: true"},{"type":"text","text":". The record’s vendor"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"identifier and trace context aren’t sent, and the standard context is sent as PostHog’s own"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"properties ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$app_version"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$device_model"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$os_name"},{"type":"text","text":" and the like)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Properties are read through the event’s schema in the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrackingPlan"},{"text":" the encoder is made with. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sensitive"},{"text":" value is never sent, whatever the record reveals, and a property whose name starts with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$"},{"text":" or is ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"distinct_id"},{"text":" is left out and logged. A record the encoder can’t write is left out and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the rest of the batch is sent: one the plan doesn’t describe, one whose event name starts with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one whose event isn’t ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Encodable"},{"text":", one holding a value JSON can’t, one whose timestamp has no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"ISO 8601 form (NaN, infinite, or more than ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int64.max"},{"text":" milliseconds from 1970), and one too large","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"for PostHog’s event limit. The destination reports each as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDropReport.skipped(_:)"},{"text":", a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SkippedRecord"},{"text":" whose","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reason is a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogEncodingError","type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"To send to TraffluentCollector, use ","type":"text"},{"code":"CollectorBatchEncoder","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"code":"CollectorEncoding","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":")","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"instead.","type":"text"}]},{"code":["import HTTPDestinations","import PostHogEncoding","import TrackingPlans","","let plan = try TrackingPlan()","let postHog = try HTTPDestination.postHog(","    projectToken: projectToken,","    host: postHogHost,  \/\/ https:\/\/us.i.posthog.com, https:\/\/eu.i.posthog.com or your own","    plan: plan)","let tracker = Tracker(enrichers: [.sessions()])","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: postHog)"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The guide "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"covers what PostHog receives, and why, in more detail."}]}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Framework","title":"PostHogEncoding","role":"collection","modules":[{"name":"PostHogEncoding"}],"externalID":"PostHogEncoding","symbolKind":"module"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/posthogencoding"]}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"references":{"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations":{"title":"HTTPDestinations","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations","type":"topic","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations","abstract":[{"text":"Send each batch of records to an HTTP endpoint, and send it again until it arrives.","type":"text"}]},"doc://PostHogEncoding/documentation/PostHogEncoding/PostHogSetupError":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogSetupError","kind":"symbol",